    check: update 0.15.2 -> commit 35d9cc0
    
    check 0.15.2 always compiles its `clock_gettime()` fallback,
    regardless of whether the target already provides it. Current
    mingw-w64/winpthreads declares `clock_gettime()` via `pthread_time.h`,
    so the fallback collides with it and the build fails with
    `redefinition of 'clock_gettime'`.
    
    Upstream fixed this after 0.15.2 (which is still the latest tagged
    release) with commit libcheck/check@bcb753f by detecting the existing
    function and skipping the fallback when present.
    
    Update check to the latest commit libcheck/check@35d9cc0

